ifferential and elevated LAP reduce likelihood of acute myeloid blast proliferation (B1), moderately supporting B2 and disfavoring B1."], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP strongly contradicts CML as a representative of B2, disfavoring it but not excluding the broader chronic myeloproliferative category."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.005430963908071526, "posterior": 0.0035369619644941403, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of lymphoid blasts and lymphadenopathy weakens lymphoid blast proliferation (e.g., ALL) as the cause. This moderately disfavors B3."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.05891697896365915, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Hypercalcemia and constitutional symptoms are more typical of lymphoid/plasma cell disorders than reactive leukocytosis. This moderately supports B4 and disfav…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of expected findings for multiple myeloma (e.g., M-spike) moderately disfavors B4 a