rterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) with Elevated Leukocyte Alkaline Phosphatase:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Acute Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (ALL):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, bleeding, bone pain\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, frequent urination, hypercalcemia\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs CML Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) with Elevated Leukocyte Alkaline Phosphatase:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Acute Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (ALL):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain"}
